CLAUDE.md

# The vendored AVR toolchain, 45 MB, built by ./scripts/fetch-avr-gcc.sh.
#
# Ignored rather than committed ON PURPOSE, and this is a decision to revisit
# rather than a permanent state: Vercel deploys from git and vercel.json's
# legacy `builds` config bundles the project directory, so /compile for AVR
# parts will NOT work in production until this is committed. SDCC's 8 MB
# bin/ + share/ are committed for exactly that reason.
#
# 45 MB is 5.6x that, it lands in git history permanently, and roughly 19 MB
# of it is avr-libc headers for ~300 parts we do not support. Trimming those
# to the avr5 family would bring it near 26 MB. Worth choosing deliberately
# before it becomes irreversible.
avr/
